From 4fe1642e05fde351813733ecf1561a2f596ed03e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: UMP <ump@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/90] launcher: fix Java mods' version conflicts before Play

A required mod present at a version its mod excludes (fabric.mod.json depends predicate) is replaced by the newest Fabric 26.3 Modrinth version when that fits; the old jar is kept as .jar.disabled. When none fits, or two mods 'break' each other, the player is told in a plain sentence which mod to update or take out. Modrinth lookup also tries '<id>-api' (Architectury) and skips ids a jar downloaded in the same round provides (Balm provides balm-fabric). Example java_deps_folder runs it on any folder for tests.

Tested: top100 minus 6 libraries -> all 5 needed ones downloaded in 13 s (one was jar-in-jar provided); old Balm in a folder -> updated, old kept disabled; second runs find nothing to do. Unit tests: outdated, clashes.
